{"id":"earth","name":"Earth","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:earth"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Earth","text":"(1.) In the sense of soil or ground, the translation of the word adamah’. In Gen. 9:20 “husbandman” is literally “man of the ground or earth.” Altars were to be built of earth (Ex. 20:24). Naaman asked for two mules’ burden of earth (2 Kings 5:17), under the superstitious notion that Jehovah, like the gods of the heathen, could be acceptably worshipped only on his own soil. (2). As the rendering of ’erets, it means the whole world (Gen. 1:2); the land as opposed to the sea (1:10). Erets also denotes a country (21:32); a plot of ground (23:15); the ground on which a man stands (33:3); the inhabitants of the earth (6:1; 11:1); all the world except Israel (2 Chr. 13:9). In the New Testament “the earth” denotes the land of Judea (Matt. 23:35); also things carnal in contrast with things heavenly (John 3:31; Col. 3:1, 2)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G3772","lemma":"οὐρανός","xlit":"ouranós","gloss":"the sky","kjv":"air, heaven, sky","count":21,"share":0.2},{"strong":"H8064","lemma":"שָׁמַיִם","xlit":"shâmayim","gloss":"the sky","kjv":"air, astrologer, heaven","count":19,"share":0.18},{"strong":"G1093","lemma":"γῆ","xlit":"gē","gloss":"soil","kjv":"country, earth, ground, land","count":16,"share":0.15},{"strong":"G3928","lemma":"παρέρχομαι","xlit":"parérchomai","gloss":"to come near or aside","kjv":"come, go, pass, past","count":8,"share":0.08},{"strong":"H5769","lemma":"עוֹלָם","xlit":"ʻôwlâm","gloss":"concealed","kjv":"alway, ancient, any more, continuance","count":10,"share":0.09},{"strong":"G2250","lemma":"ἡμέρα","xlit":"hēméra","gloss":"the time space between dawn and dark, or the whole 24 ho","kjv":"age, + alway, day ), + for ever","count":9,"share":0.08}],"verses":["Matt.5.18","Matt.24.29","Matt.24.30","Matt.24.31","Matt.24.35","Matt.24.36","Mark.13.25","Mark.13.27","Mark.13.31","Mark.13.32","Luke.21.26","Luke.21